{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>For I have known him, that he may command</b> — This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 18:19): \"אֲרֵי יְדַעְתִּנֵּיהּ\" ('for I have known him'), as in its Targum translation — an expression of endearment, like \"מוֹדָע לְאִישָׁהּ\" (Ruth 2:1, 'kinsman to her husband'), \"וָאֵדָעֲךָ\" (Exodus 33:17, 'and I have known you'). Now the essence of all of them is the language of knowledge, for one who endears a person and draws him near knows him and is familiar with him. And if you interpret it as 'I know of him that he will command his sons,' then 'לְמַעַן' ('that' / 'in order that') does not fit the expression. And it is possible that 'יְדַעְתִּיו' means 'I have raised him and exalted him,' for the sake of 'that he may command his children after him to do what is right before Me,' and therefore 'I will make of him a great and mighty nation' that will serve Me. Similar to it: \"יְדַעְתִּיךָ בְּשֵׁם\" (Exodus 33:12, 'I have known you by name'), \"מָה אָדָם וַתֵּדָעֵהוּ\" (Psalms 144:3, 'what is man that You take note of him'). Or he says: 'I have known him that he will command,' similar to \"לְמַעַן יָנוּחַ שׁוֹרְךָ וַחֲמֹרֶךָ\" (Exodus 23:12, 'so that your ox and your donkey may rest') — that they shall rest. But the correct interpretation in my eyes is that it is actual knowledge of him. It alludes to the fact that the knowledge of HaShem — which is His providence over the lowly world — is to watch over the generalities, and even human beings are left within it for the incidental occurrences until the time of their reckoning arrives; but regarding His devout ones, He sets His attention upon them to know them in particular, so that His watchful care cleaves to them constantly, and the knowledge and mindfulness of them never depart from them at all, in the sense of \"לֹא יִגְרַע מִצַּדִּיק עֵינָיו\" (Job 36:7, 'He does not withdraw His eyes from the righteous'). And from this many verses come, as it is written (Psalms 33:18): \"הִנֵּה עֵין ה' אֶל יְרֵאָיו\" ('Behold, the eye of HaShem is upon those who fear Him'), and others like it."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:31:26.639701546Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}